summary:
Segment covers origin/codex/multimodal-layer-20260927 (tip b514595f, last tested code 808ad32f; 23 commits since handoff-history-20260909). It is Codex's continuation of Vyakti with two halves.

(1) A multimodal evidence layer (Sep 27-29). Stored text, document, audio-transcript and video-transcript evidence reaches the claim extractor and the owner review UI with honest modality, locator and limitation descriptors. It fixed a Number(null) zero-timestamp bug. Images are refused as semantics; there is no vision model at all.

(2) Hardening of the common-friend Group AI (Sep 29 - Oct 1). This is an AI persona that is a member of a Telegram group of 2-6 linked adults. Consent comes from admin promotion. Privacy is a SQL disclosure predicate over immutable per-turn episode participants. Speaking is decided in code (lurk/react/speak on explicit address only). There is a per-addressee honorific roster, app-voiced cards and commands, and negotiated forgetting.

New this branch:
- portable dependency-free checkpoint kernel (A/S/A/S re-reads, sticky invalidation);
- complete Telegram audience witness;
- attributed source-turn selector with whole-payload byte budgets (lexical recall measured and NOT promoted: 27/54 vs 0/54, but 0/27 under adversarial distractors);
- truthful delivery outcomes;
- known-consent source-time fence in JS and SQL;
- keyless hosted synthetic-PostgreSQL SQL proof (50 groups);
- a 44 px touch-target fix with a negative-control test;
- five research/audit reports (Honcho, portable layer, durability, native identity, recall).

Final state: release 24/24 on Node 22 and 24, SQL50 and APK pass. But no real transport, provider or human group task ever ran. Live vy_group had 0 rows. Native web group identity/UI, grant writer, group media, durable dedup and dependent forgetting remain open, and two owner policy questions are unanswered. The handoff itself records that process overhead displaced real user journeys.

For Taxila, the most valuable reusable pieces are: the disclosure predicate plus per-turn episode ACL (sibling/parent privacy), the checkpoint kernel, truthful delivery, the consent-time fence, the participation decision and roster (to be inverted to teacher-led), modality-honest evidence descriptors, source-aware claim review, and the evaluation/CI patterns. The adult gate must invert into a parental-consent gate.
